('0fd50dba-a2bc-55d9-8533-38ba145a5a4f', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', 'ac0eb546-c37c-5122-8eaa-89bbcb42a5c1', 'a-level', '19.2', '9702 coursebook 19.2 · The first law of thermodynamics', 27, 27, 'A gas is compressed at a constant 3.0 × 10⁵ Pa from 0.050 m³ to 0.035 m³ while losing 2500 J by heating. Calculate ΔU.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2000', 'J', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'w = +pΔV = 3.0 × 10⁵ × 0.015 = 4500 J. q = −2500 J. ΔU = −2500 + 4500 = 2000 J. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: volume change 0.015 m³. C1: w positive (compression). C1: q negative. A1: ΔU = 2000 J.', 4, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg9da2a982-t fg9da2a982-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg9da2a982-t">Compression at constant pressure</title><desc id="fg9da2a982-d">p–V graph: a horizontal line at 3.0 × 10⁵ Pa from 0.050 m³ to 0.035 m³; the shaded area is the work done on the gas.</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="83.7" y1="34" x2="83.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="143.3" y1="34" x2="143.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="203" y1="34" x2="203" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="262.7" y1="34" x2="262.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="322.3" y1="34" x2="322.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="3