ints="332.8,184.2 168.9,184.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="162.9" y="192.2" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">A</text><text x="162.9" y="68.7" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">B</text><text x="338.8" y="176.2" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">C</text></svg>', 'p–V diagram of cycle ABCA: A to B is a vertical line (constant volume, 500 J supplied), B to C is an isothermal expansion curve (350 J of work done by the gas), and C to A is a horizontal compression at 1.0 × 10⁵ Pa by 2.0 × 10⁻³ m³.'),
('d4a79119-ed29-53ae-be5a-345821cfaba7', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', 'ac0eb546-c37c-5122-8eaa-89bbcb42a5c1', 'a-level', '19.2', '9702 coursebook 19.2 · The first law of thermodynamics', 43, 43, 'An ideal gas at 1.2 × 10⁵ Pa is heated at constant pressure and its volume increases from 3.0 × 10⁻³ m³ to 4.5 × 10⁻³ m³. For this gas, ΔU = 1.5pΔV at constant pressure. (a) Calculate the work done by the gas. (b) Calculate ΔU. (c) Calculate the heat supplied. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '450', 'J', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) W = pΔV = 1.2 × 10⁵ × 1.5 × 10⁻³ = 180 J. (b) ΔU = 1.5 × 180 = 270 J. (c) q = ΔU − w = 270 − (−180) = 450 J. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: W = pΔV. A1: W. A1: ΔU. C1: q = ΔU − w. A1: q = 450 J.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('5eca5171-3dd0-571b-b046-7b2e2b07e483', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', 'ac0eb546-c37c-5122-8eaa-89bbcb42a5c1', 'a-level', '19.2', '9702 coursebook 19.2 · The first law of thermodynamics', 44, 44, 'In a refrigerator, a refrigerant gas is compressed adiabatically (300 J of work done on it), then loses 820 J by heating in the condenser at roughly constant volume, then expands, absorbing 520 J from the food compartment while doing no external work. (a) Calculate ΔU for each stage. (b) Show that the net ΔU over the cycle is zero. (c) Calculate the net energy transferred to the room by heating per cycle. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '820', 'J', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) Compression: ΔU = +300 J. Condenser: ΔU = −820 J. Expansion: ΔU = +520 J. (b) 300 − 820 + 520 = 0. (c) The room receives 520 + 300 = 820 J per cycle (the heat taken from the food plus the work done). Mark scheme (6 marks). A1: stage 1. A1: stage 2. A1: stage 3. M1: sum zero. B1: 820 J to the room. B1: equals heat removed + work.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('814ed11b-d1d5-536c-9978-6c9affc3654e', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', 'ac0eb546-c37c-5122-8eaa-89bbcb42a5c1', 'a-level', '19.2', '9702 coursebook 19.2 · The first law of thermodynamics', 45, 45, 'A student compresses air in a bicycle pump: the handle moves 20 cm against an average force of 150 N, so quickly that no heat escapes. (a) Calculate the work done on the air. (b) State ΔU. (c) The air (0.0050 mol) has ΔU = 1.5nRΔT (monatomic model). Calculate the temperature rise. Give only the answer to (c). Take R = 8.31 J K⁻¹ mol⁻¹.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '481.3', 'K', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) w = Fd = 150 × 0.20 = 30 J. (b) q = 0, so ΔU = +30 J. (c) ΔT = ΔU/(1.5nR) = 30 ÷ (1.5 × 0.0050 × 8.31) = 481 K (real air is diatomic, so the rise is less). Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: w = Fd. A1: 30 J. B1: ΔU = w. C1: ΔU = 1.5nRΔT. A1: ΔT = 481 K.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('dea924f8-ecf8-5a8a-ab0b-2c6ef7009e61', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', 'ac0eb546-c37c-5122-8eaa-89bbcb42a5c1', 'a-level', '19.2', '9702 coursebook 19.2 · The first law of thermodynamics', 46, 46, 'A gas follows a straight-line path on a p–V diagram from (1.0 × 10⁻³ m³, 3.0 × 10⁵ Pa) to (4.0 × 10⁻³ m³, 1.0 × 10⁵ Pa). Its internal energy at the start and end is the same. (a) Calculate the work done by the gas (area of the trapezium). (b) State ΔU. (c) Calculate the heat supplied. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '600', 'J', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) Area = ½(3.0 × 10⁵ + 1.0 × 10⁵) × 3.0 × 10⁻³ = 600 J. (b) ΔU = 0. (c) q = ΔU − w = 0 − (−600) = 600 J. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: trapezium area. A1: 600 J. B1: ΔU = 0. C1: q = ΔU − w. C1: w negative for expansion. A1: q = 600 J.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg6ad407f7-t fg6ad407f7-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg6ad407f7-t">Straight-line path</title><desc id="fg6ad407f7-d">p–V graph: a straight line from 1.0 × 10⁻³ m³ at 3.0 × 10⁵ Pa to 4.0 × 10⁻³ m³ at 1.0 × 10⁵ Pa; the shaded trapezium under it is the work done by the gas.</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="103.6" y1="34" x2="103.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="183.1" y1="34" x2="183.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="262.7" y1="34" x2="262.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="342.2" y1="34" x2="342.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="182.6" x2="382" y2="182.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="123.1" x2="382" y2="123.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="63.7" x2="382" y2="63.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="388" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="24" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,242 385.7,245 385.7,239" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="24,24 27,30.3 21,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="24" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="24" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="103.6" y1="242" x2="103.6" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="103.6" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1</text><line x1="183.1" y1="242" x2="183.1" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="183.1" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2</text><line x1="262.7" y1="242" x2="262.7" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="262.7" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">3</text><line x1="342.2" y1="242" x2="342.2" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="342.2" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4</text><line x1="20" y1="242" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="242" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="20" y1="182.6" x2="24" y2="182.6" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="182.6" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1</text><line x1="20" y1="123.1" x2="24" y2="123.1" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="123.1" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2</text><line x1="20" y1="63.7" x2="24" y2="63.7" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="63.7" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">3</text><text x="203" y="274" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">V / 10⁻³ m³</text><text x="20" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">p / 10⁵ Pa</text><polygon points="103.6,63.7 342.2,182.6 342.2,242 103.6,242" style="stroke:none;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polyline points="103.6,63.7 342.2,182.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'p–V graph: a straight line from 1.0 × 10⁻³ m³ at 3.0 × 10⁵ Pa to 4.0 × 10⁻³ m³ at 1.0 × 10⁵ Pa; the shaded trapezium under it is the work done by the gas.'),
('7cc5f305-d73b-5d97-b83b-abed48258c5d', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', 'ac0eb546-c37c-5122-8eaa-89bbcb42a5c1', 'a-level', '19.2', '9702 coursebook 19.2 · The first law of thermodynamics', 47, 47, 'A gas is heated at constant volume from A to B, receiving 300 J, then expands at constant pressure 2.0 × 10⁵ Pa from 1.0 × 10⁻³ m³ to 2.5 × 10⁻³ m³ (B to C), receiving 750 J. (a) Calculate ΔU for A to B. (b) Calculate the work done by the gas for B to C. (c) Calculate ΔU for B to C and the total ΔU from A to C. Give only the total in (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '750', 'J', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) w = 0, so ΔU = 300 J. (b) W = pΔV = 2.0 × 10⁵ × 1.5 × 10⁻³ = 300 J. (c) ΔU(BC) = 750 − 300 = 450 J. Total = 300 + 450 = 750 J. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: w = 0 at constant volume. A1: ΔU(AB). C1: W = pΔV. C1: ΔU(BC) = q + w. A1: ΔU = 750 J.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgbc570a92-t fgbc570a92-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgbc570a92-t">Two-stage change</title><desc id="fgbc570a92-d">p–V graph: A to B is a vertical line at 1.0 × 10⁻³ m³ (heated at constant volume, 300 J); B to C is a horizontal line at 2.0 × 10⁵ Pa from 1.0 × 10⁻³ m³ to 2.5 × 10⁻³ m³ (750 J supplied). The pressure at A is drawn schematically.</desc><line x1="33" y1="34" x2="33" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="91.2" y1="34" x2="91.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="149.4" y1="34" x2="149.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="207.5" y1="34" x2="207.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;st