text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">B</text><text x="329.8" y="74" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">C</text></svg>', 'p–V graph: A to B is a vertical line at 1.0 × 10⁻³ m³ (heated at constant volume, 300 J); B to C is a horizontal line at 2.0 × 10⁵ Pa from 1.0 × 10⁻³ m³ to 2.5 × 10⁻³ m³ (750 J supplied). The pressure at A is drawn schematically.'),
('1d7747f8-5369-5a85-9546-ea71c722d580', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', 'ac0eb546-c37c-5122-8eaa-89bbcb42a5c1', 'a-level', '19.2', '9702 coursebook 19.2 · The first law of thermodynamics', 48, 48, 'A heat engine takes in 2400 J per cycle from a hot source and does 600 J of work, returning to its starting state. (a) State ΔU for the cycle. (b) Calculate the heat rejected to the cold sink per cycle. (c) Calculate the efficiency, and the rate of heat rejection at 50 cycles per second. Give only the rate in (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '90000', 'W', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) ΔU = 0 for a complete cycle. (b) q_in − q_out = W, so q_out = 2400 − 600 = 1800 J. (c) Efficiency = 600 ÷ 2400 × 100 = 25 %. Rate = 1800 × 50 = 90000 W. Mark scheme (6 marks). B1: ΔU = 0. C1: energy balance. A1: 1800 J. A1: 25 %. C1: × 50. A1: P = 9.00 × 10⁴ W.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('f51790e5-1fe6-5a0f-a1a6-26556336e7fc', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', 'ac0eb546-c37c-5122-8eaa-89bbcb42a5c1', 'a-level', '19.2', '9702 coursebook 19.2 · The first law of thermodynamics', 49, 49, 'A gas expands from 1.0 × 10⁻³ m³ to 3.0 × 10⁻³ m³. On a p–V graph its pressure falls linearly from 5.0 × 10⁵ Pa to 2.0 × 10⁵ Pa. 1200 J is supplied by heating. (a) Calculate the work done by the gas from the area under the graph. (b) Calculate ΔU. (c) State whether the temperature rose or fell, assuming ideal behaviour. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '500', 'J', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) W = ½(5.0 × 10⁵ + 2.0 × 10⁵) × 2.0 × 10⁻³ = 700 J. (b) ΔU = q + w = 1200 − 700 = 500 J. (c) ΔU > 0, so the temperature rose. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: trapezium area. A1: 700 J. C1: w = −700 J. A1: ΔU = 500 J. B1: temperature rose.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg4f4625e9-t fg4f4625e9-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg4f4625e9-t">Linear p–V path</title><desc id="fg4f4625e9-d">p–V graph: the pressure falls linearly from 5.0 × 10⁵ Pa at 1.0 × 10⁻³ m³ to 2.0 × 10⁵ Pa at 3.0 × 10⁻³ m³; the shaded area is the work done by the gas.</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="126.3" y1="34" x2="126.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="228.6" y1="34" x2="228.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="330.9" y1="34" x2="330.9" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="204.9" x2="382" y2="204.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="167.7" x2="382" y2="167.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="130.6" x2="382" y2="130.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="93.4" x2="382" y2="93.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="56.3" x2="382" y2="56.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="388" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="24" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,242 385.7,245 385.7,239" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="24,24 27,30.3 21,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="24" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="24" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="126.3" y1="242" x2="126.3" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="126.3" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1</text><line x1="228.6" y1="242" x2="228.6" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="228.6" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2</text><line x1="330.9" y1="242" x2="330.9" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="330.9" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">3</text><line x1="20" y1="242" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="242" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="20" y1="204.9" x2="24" y2="204.9" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="204.9" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1</text><line x1="20" y1="167.7" x2="24" y2="167.7" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="167.7" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2</text><line x1="20" y1="130.6" x2="24" y2="130.6" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="130.6" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">3</text><line x1="20" y1="93.4" x2="24" y2="93.4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="93.4" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4</text><line x1="20" y1="56.3" x2="24" y2="56.3" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="56.3" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">5</text><text x="203" y="274" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">V / 10⁻³ m³</text><text x="20" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">p / 10⁵ Pa</text><polygon points="126.3,56.3 330.9,167.7 330.9,242 126.3,242" style="stroke:none;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polyline points="126.3,56.3 330.9,167.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'p–V graph: the pressure falls linearly from 5.0 × 10⁵ Pa at 1.0 × 10⁻³ m³ to 2.0 × 10⁵ Pa at 3.0 × 10⁻³ m³; the shaded area is the work done by the gas.'),
('0af297f3-5af0-57ff-9feb-6e29217157af', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', 'ac0eb546-c37c-5122-8eaa-89bbcb42a5c1', 'a-level', '19.2', '9702 coursebook 19.2 · The first law of thermodynamics', 50, 50, 'A gas in a cylinder at 1.0 × 10⁵ Pa occupies 2.4 × 10⁻³ m³. It is compressed at constant pressure to 1.6 × 10⁻³ m³ while 140 J leaves by heating, and then heated at constant volume with 260 J. (a) Calculate the work done on the gas in the first stage. (b) Calculate ΔU for each stage. (c) Calculate the total ΔU. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '200', 'J', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) w = pΔV = 1.0 × 10⁵ × 0.8 × 10⁻³ = 80 J (on the gas). (b) Stage 1: ΔU = −140 + 80 = −60 J. Stage 2: w = 0, ΔU = 260 J. (c) total = −60 + 260 = 200 J. Mark scheme (5 marks). A1: w = 80 J. C1: stage 1 ΔU. C1: stage 2 w = 0. A1: stage values. A1: ΔU = 200 J.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fge3e28b44-t fge3e28b44-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fge3e28b44-t">Compression then heating</title><desc id="fge3e28b44-d">p–V graph: compression at a constant 1.0 × 10⁵ Pa from 2.4 × 10⁻³ m³ to 1.6 × 10⁻³ m³ (shaded area: work done on the gas), then heating at constant volume, shown as a vertical line rising at 1.6 × 10⁻³ m³.</desc><line x1="33" y1="34" x2="33" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="79.6" y1="34" x2="79.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="126.1" y1="34" x2="126.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="172.6" y1="34" x2="172.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;st