e x1="29" y1="242" x2="33" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="242" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="29" y1="190" x2="33" y2="190" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="190" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.5</text><line x1="29" y1="138" x2="33" y2="138" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="138" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.0</text><line x1="29" y1="86" x2="33" y2="86" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="86" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.5</text><line x1="29" y1="34" x2="33" y2="34" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="34" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2.0</text><text x="207.5" y="274" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">V / 10⁻³ m³</text><text x="29" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">p / 10⁵ Pa</text><polygon points="219.2,138 312.2,138 312.2,242 219.2,242" style="stroke:none;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polyline points="312.2,138 219.2,138 219.2,75.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'p–V graph: compression at a constant 1.0 × 10⁵ Pa from 2.4 × 10⁻³ m³ to 1.6 × 10⁻³ m³ (shaded area: work done on the gas), then heating at constant volume, shown as a vertical line rising at 1.6 × 10⁻³ m³.'),
('a836afd8-d6b4-53e9-a3ca-1e05e907d364', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', 'ac0eb546-c37c-5122-8eaa-89bbcb42a5c1', 'a-level', '19.2', '9702 coursebook 19.2 · The first law of thermodynamics', 51, 51, 'An inflatable mattress is pumped up. The pump does 3.2 kJ of work on the air, and the air does 1.8 kJ of work pushing back the atmosphere as the mattress swells. The air loses 0.6 kJ by heating. (a) Calculate the net work done on the air. (b) Calculate ΔU of the air. (c) Explain whether the air ends up warmer or cooler than at the start. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '800', 'J', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) w = 3200 − 1800 = 1400 J. (b) ΔU = q + w = −600 + 1400 = 800 J. (c) ΔU > 0 for the air that entered (an ideal-gas model links U to T), so it is warmer. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: net w. A1: 1400 J. C1: ΔU = q + w. A1: 800 J. B1: warmer. B1: reason.', 6, NULL, NULL)
