 y2="82" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="82" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">20</text><line x1="25.4" y1="42" x2="29.4" y2="42" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="42" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">25</text><text x="205.7" y="274" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">θ / °C</text><text x="25.4" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">column length / cm</text><line x1="29.4" y1="122" x2="382" y2="122" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/><text x="380" y="112" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">15.0 cm</text><polyline points="29.4,210 349.9,50" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'Calibration graph of column length against temperature: a straight line from 4.0 cm at 0 °C to 24.0 cm at 100 °C. A dashed line marks 15.0 cm.'),
('06343e9d-f899-537d-835c-2c88bb36eac7', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', '44937e02-ca76-55a2-936f-ebfb890a9d89', 'a-level', '19.5', '9702 coursebook 19.5 · Temperature scales', 26, 26, 'A thermistor and a resistance-wire thermometer are calibrated at 0 °C and 100 °C. At 50 °C (measured by a gas thermometer) they read different values. Why?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Their resistances do not vary linearly with temperature in the same way, so a linear scale between fixed points gives different readings', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Scales based on different thermometric properties agree only at the fixed points unless each property varies linearly with true temperature. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: different property–temperature relations. C1: non-linear. C1: agree only at fixed points. A1: B (Their resistances do not vary linearly with temperature in the same way, so a linear scale between fixed points gives different readings).', 4, NULL, NULL),
('45793e4b-d644-5e15-9c2f-a58cee41513e', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', '44937e02-ca76-55a2-936f-ebfb890a9d89', 'a-level', '19.5', '9702 coursebook 19.5 · Temperature scales', 27, 27, 'A gas thermometer at constant volume shows a pressure of 1.00 × 10⁵ Pa at the triple point of water (273.16 K). In a hot liquid the pressure is 1.36 × 10⁵ Pa. Calculate the temperature of the liquid in kelvin.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '371.5', 'K', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'T = 273.16 × p/p_tr = 273.16 × 1.36 ÷ 1.00 = 371.5 K. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: T ∝ p at constant volume. C1: substitution. A1: T = 371 K.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('515965eb-bb15-5f01-b59b-c22ddd2fb3d0', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', '44937e02-ca76-55a2-936f-ebfb890a9d89', 'a-level', '19.5', '9702 coursebook 19.5 · Temperature scales', 28, 28, 'A thermocouple gives 0.0 mV at 0 °C and 4.1 mV at 100 °C. Assuming a linear response, calculate the temperature when the e.m.f. is 2.9 mV, and convert it to kelvin. Give the temperature in kelvin.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '343.9', 'K', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'θ = 2.9 ÷ 4.1 × 100 = 70.7 °C. T = 70.73 + 273.15 = 344 K. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: linear interpolation. C1: °C. C1: + 273.15. A1: T = 344 K.', 4, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgd06ba891-t fgd06ba891-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgd06ba891-t">Thermocouple calibration</title><desc id="fgd06ba891-d">Calibration graph of thermocouple e.m.f. against temperature: a straight line from 0.0 mV at 0 °C to 4.1 mV at 100 °C. A dashed line marks 2.9 mV.</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="89.1" y1="34" x2="89.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="154.2" y1="34" x2="154.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="219.3" y1="34" x2="219.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="284.4" y1="34" x2="284.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="349.5" y1="34" x2="349.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;s