l:currentColor">40</text><line x1="219.3" y1="242" x2="219.3" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="219.3" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">60</text><line x1="284.4" y1="242" x2="284.4" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="284.4" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">80</text><line x1="349.5" y1="242" x2="349.5" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="349.5" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">100</text><line x1="20" y1="242" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="242" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="20" y1="196.8" x2="24" y2="196.8" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="196.8" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1</text><line x1="20" y1="151.6" x2="24" y2="151.6" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="151.6" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2</text><line x1="20" y1="106.3" x2="24" y2="106.3" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="106.3" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">3</text><line x1="20" y1="61.1" x2="24" y2="61.1" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="61.1" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4</text><text x="203" y="274" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">θ / °C</text><text x="20" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">E / mV</text><line x1="24" y1="110.9" x2="382" y2="110.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/><text x="380" y="100.9" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2.9 mV</text><polyline points="24,242 349.5,56.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'Calibration graph of thermocouple e.m.f. against temperature: a straight line from 0.0 mV at 0 °C to 4.1 mV at 100 °C. A dashed line marks 2.9 mV.'),
('1d518e3a-ea04-5b86-935f-13fe231e7800', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', '44937e02-ca76-55a2-936f-ebfb890a9d89', 'a-level', '19.5', '9702 coursebook 19.5 · Temperature scales', 29, 29, 'Which statement about the kelvin and Celsius scales is correct?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'A temperature difference has the same value in K and in °C', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'T(K) = θ(°C) + 273.15: values differ by 273.15, but intervals are equal. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: equal intervals. C1: offset 273.15. A1: C (A temperature difference has the same value in K and in °C).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('e61642ec-6ecb-5d1d-8b3e-cd94fae069b8', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', '44937e02-ca76-55a2-936f-ebfb890a9d89', 'a-level', '19.5', '9702 coursebook 19.5 · Temperature scales', 30, 30, 'The temperature of a gas doubles from 300 K. What is its new temperature in °C?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '327', '°C', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'New T = 2 × 300 = 600 K. θ = 600 − 273 = 327 °C. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: double the kelvin value. C1: convert. A1: θ = 327 °C.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('c95325dc-7ae0-57c8-ad76-927f4180bb9e', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', '44937e02-ca76-55a2-936f-ebfb890a9d89', 'a-level', '19.5', '9702 coursebook 19.5 · Temperature scales', 31, 31, 'A student says that heating water from 10 °C to 20 °C "doubles its temperature". Why is this wrong?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'In kelvin the temperature rises from 283 K to 293 K, only about 3.5 % higher', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Ratios of temperatures are only meaningful on an absolute scale: 293 ÷ 283 = 1.035. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: convert to kelvin. C1: ratio 1.035. C1: absolute scale needed for ratios. A1: A (In kelvin the temperature rises from 283 K to 293 K, only about 3.5 % higher).', 4, NULL, NULL),
('22d43b0c-659f-59a9-83bb-0e645caf2d95', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', '44937e02-ca76-55a2-936f-ebfb890a9d89', 'a-level', '19.5', '9702 coursebook 19.5 · Temperature scales', 32, 32, 'A platinum resistance thermometer reads 108.0 Ω in a cold bath and 136.0 Ω in boiling water (100 °C). Its resistance at 0 °C is 100.0 Ω. Calculate the cold bath temperature on the platinum scale.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '22.22', '°C', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'θ = (108.0 − 100.0) ÷ (136.0 − 100.0) × 100 = 22.2 °C. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: interpolation. C1: substitution. A1: θ = 22.2 °C.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg020cc259-t fg020cc259-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg020cc259-t">Platinum scale</title><desc id="fg020cc259-d">Calibration graph for the platinum scale: a straight line from 100.0 Ω at 0 °C to 136.0 Ω at 100 °C. A dashed line marks the cold-bath reading, 108.0 Ω.</desc><line x1="36.2" y1="34" x2="36.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="99" y1="34" x2="99" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="161.9" y1="34" x2="161.9" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="224.8" y1="34" x2="224.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="287.7" y1="34" x2="287.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="350.6" y1="34" x2="350.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="36.2" y1="218.9" x2="382" y2="218.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="36.2" y1="172.7" x2="382" y2="172.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="36.2" y1="126.4" x2="382" y2="126.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="36.2" y1="80.2" x2="382" y2="80.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="36.2" y1="34" x2="382" y2="34" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="36.2" y1="242" x2="388" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="36.2" y1="242" x2="36.2" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,242 385.7,245 385.7,239" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="36.2,24 39.1,30.3 33.2,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="36.2" y1="242" x2="36.2" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="36.2" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="99" y1="242" x2="99" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="99" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">20</text><line x1="161.9" y1="242" x2="161.9" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="161.9" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">40</text><line x1="224.8" y1="242" x2="224.8" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="224.8" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">60</text><line x1="287.7" y1="242" x2="287.7" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="287.7" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">80</text><line x1="350.6" y1="242" x2="350.6" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="350.6" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">100</text><line x1="32.2" y1="218.9" x2="36.2" y2="218.9" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="29.2" y="218.9" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">100</text><line x1="32.2" y1="172.7" x2="36.2" y2="172.7" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="29.2" y="172.7" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">110</text><line x1="32.2" y1="126.4" x2="36.2" y2="126.4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="29.2" y="126.4" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">120</text><line x1="32.2" y1="80.2" x2="36.2" y2="80.2" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="29.2" y="80.2" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">130</text><line x1="32.2" y1="34" x2="36.2" y2="34" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="29.2" y="34" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">140</text><text x="209.1" y="274" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">θ / °C</text><text x="32.2" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">R / Ω</text><line x1="36.2" y1="181.9" x2="382" y2="181.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/><text x="380" y="171.9" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">108.0 Ω</text><polyline points="36.2,218.9 350.6,52.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'Calibration graph for the platinum scale: a straight line from 100.0 Ω at 0 °C to 136.0 Ω at 100 °C. A dashed line marks the cold-bath reading, 108.0 Ω.'),
('9a51fc2b-042a-5578-a888-f8cf3ced82c0', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', '44937e02-ca76-55a2-936f-ebfb890a9d89', 'a-level', '19.5', '9702 coursebook 19.5 · Temperature scales', 33, 33, 'Which of these is NOT a suitable thermometric property?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The mass of an object', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Mass does not change with temperature, so it cannot indicate temperature. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: must vary with temperature. C1: mass does not. A1: D (The mass of an object).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('e504c726-72fb-5597-8625-9807b5716107', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', '44937e02-ca76-55a2-936f-ebfb890a9d89', 'a-level', '19.5', '9702 coursebook 19.5 · Temperature scales', 34, 34, 'A constant-pressure gas thermometer has a volume of 250 cm³ at 0 °C (273 K). At an unknown temperature the volume is 340 cm³. Calculate the temperature in °C.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '98.28', '°C', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'T ∝ V: T = 273 × 340 ÷ 250 = 371.3 K. θ = 371.3 − 273 = 98.3 °C. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: V ∝ T. C1: T in K. C1: convert. A1: θ = 98.3 °C.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('d272ee8c-8e2b-5369-a5e4-30f4b92c4082', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', '44937e02-ca76-55a2-936f-ebfb890a9d89', 'a-level', '19.5', '9702 coursebook 19.5 · Temperature scales', 35, 35, 'Why is a thermocouple, rather than a liquid-in-glass thermometer, used to measure the temperature of a furnace at 1200 °C?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It can work at very high temperatures and gives an electrical output that responds quickly', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Glass and liquids fail at high temperature; a thermocouple of suitable metals survives and responds fast. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: high temperature range. C1: fast/electrical output. A1: B (It can work at very high temperatures and gives an electrical output that responds quickly).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('4bdd3917-b9b8-5c02-9907-6a380c17c81f', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', '44937e02-ca76-55a2-936f-ebfb890a9d89', 'a-level', '19.5', '9702 coursebook 19.5 · Temperature scales', 36, 36, 'A temperature of 77 K is measured in liquid nitrogen. By how many kelvin must it be warmed to reach 20 °C?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '216', 'K', false, NULL, false, NULL, '20 °C = 293 K, so ΔT = 293 − 77 = 216 K. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: convert 20 °C. C1: difference. A1: ΔT = 216 K.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('1cc51356-c96d-5502-8747-cba04ab820c4', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', '44937e02-ca76-55a2-936f-ebfb890a9d89', 'a-level', '19.5', '9702 coursebook 19.5 · Temperature scales', 37, 37, 'On an empirical scale based on a gas thermometer, T = 273.16 × (p/p_tr). Find the pressure ratio p/p_tr at the boiling point of water (373.15 K).', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.366', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'p/p_tr = T/273.16 = 373.15 ÷ 273.16 = 1.366. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: rearranged. C1: substitution. A1: ratio = 1.366.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('0a2251a8-664b-5e5f-93b1-bd9671bc00ef', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', '44937e02-ca76-55a2-936f-ebfb890a9d89', 'a-level', '19.5', '9702 coursebook 19.5 · Temperature scales', 38, 38, 'Two thermometers based on different properties are both calibrated at the ice and steam points. When might they disagree?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'At temperatures between and beyond the fixed points, if their properties vary non-linearly', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Calibration forces agreement only at the fixed points. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: agree at fixed points. C1: may disagree elsewhere. A1: C (At temperatures between and beyond the fixed points, if their properties vary non-linearly).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('77c52f1d-0e69-5712-b615-79c8c8121a70', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', '44937e02-ca76-55a2-936f-ebfb890a9d89', 'a-level', '19.5', '9702 coursebook 19.5 · Temperature scales', 39, 39, 'A thermistor has resistance 5.0 kΩ at 0 °C and 0.50 kΩ at 100 °C. At an unknown temperature it reads 1.5 kΩ. (a) Calculate the temperature assuming a linear scale. (b) The true temperature (from a gas thermometer) is 46 °C. Explain the difference. (c) State one advantage and one disadvantage of a thermistor. Give only the answer to (a).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '77.78', '°C', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) θ = (5.0 − 1.5) ÷ (5.0 − 0.50) × 100 = 77.8 °C. (b) The thermistor''s resistance varies non-linearly (roughly exponentially) with temperature, so a linear scale between the fixed points is wrong. (c) Advantage: very sensitive/fast. Disadvantage: non-linear, needs calibration. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: linear interpolation (resistance falls). A1: θ = 77.8 °C. B1: non-linear. B1: advantage. B1: disadvantage.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgeecf6933-t fgeecf6933-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgeecf6933-t">Linear-scale assumption</title><desc id="fgeecf6933-d">Graph of thermistor resistance against temperature assuming a linear scale: a straight line from 5.0 kΩ at 0 °C to 0.50 kΩ at 100 °C. A dashed line marks 1.5 kΩ.</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="89.1" y1="34" x2="89.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="154.2" y1="34" x2="154.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="219.3" y1="34" x2="219.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="284.4" y1="34" x2="284.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="349.5" y1="34" x2="349.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="204.2" x2="382" y2="204.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="166.4" x2="382" y2="166.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="128.5" x2="382" y2="128.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="90.7" x2="382" y2="90.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="52.9" x2="382" y2="52.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="388" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="24" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,242 385.7,245 385.7,239" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="24,24 27,30.3 21,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="24" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="24" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="89.1" y1="242" x2="89.1" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="89.1" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">20</text><line x1="154.2" y1="242" x2="154.2" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="154.2" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">40</text><line x1="219.3" y1="242" x2="219.3" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="219.3" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">60</text><line x1="284.4" y1="242" x2="284.4" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="284.4" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">80</text><line x1="349.5" y1="242" x2="349.5" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="349.5" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">100</text><line x1="20" y1="242" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="242" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="20" y1="204.2" x2="24" y2="204.2" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="204.2" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1</text><line x1="20" y1="166.4" x2="24" y2="166.4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="166.4" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2</text><line x1="20" y1="128.5" x2="24" y2="128.5" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="128.5" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">3</text><line x1="20" y1="90.7" x2="24" y2="90.7" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="90.7" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4</text><line x1="20" y1="52.9" x2="24" y2="52.9" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="52.9" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">5</text><text x="203" y="274" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">θ / °C</text><text x="20" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">R / kΩ</text><line x1="24" y1="185.3" x2="382" y2="185.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/><text x="380" y="175.3" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.5 kΩ</text><polyline points="24,52.9 349.5,223.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'Graph of thermistor resistance against temperature assuming a linear scale: a straight line from 5.0 kΩ at 0 °C to 0.50 kΩ at 100 °C. A dashed line marks 1.5 kΩ.'),
('c426f35c-1533-5a72-810f-03180e166823', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', '44937e02-ca76-55a2-936f-ebfb890a9d89', 'a-level', '19.5', '9702 coursebook 19.5 · Temperature scales', 40, 40, 'A constant-volume gas thermometer reads p = 1.098 × 10⁵ Pa at the triple point of water (273.16 K) and 1.500 × 10⁵ Pa in a liquid. (a) Calculate the temperature of the liquid in K. (b) Convert it to °C. (c) Explain why the gas thermometer is used to calibrate other thermometers. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '100', '°C', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) T = 273.16 × 1.500 ÷ 1.098 = 373.2 K. (b) θ = 373.2 − 273.15 = 100 °C. (c) An ideal gas thermometer agrees with the thermodynamic scale, independent of the gas used, at low pressure. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: T ∝ p. A1: T. C1: subtract 273.15. A1: θ = 100 °C. B1: matches thermodynamic scale. B1: independent of gas.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('a512fb99-89be-5a0d-a9db-c1733ed12d45', '732e83dd-2c22-497f-8d64-2f7a3fd69629', '44937e02-ca76-55a2-936f-ebfb890a9d89', 'a-level', '19.5', '9702 coursebook 19.5 · Temperature scales', 41, 41, 'A thermocouple''s e.m.f. follows E = aθ + bθ², with a = 40 µV K⁻¹ and b = 0.040 µV K⁻² (θ in °C). (a) Calculate E at 100 °C. (b) Calculate E at 50 °C. (c) Find the temperature a linear scale calibrated at 0 and 100 °C would show when the true temperature is 50 °C. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '47.73', '°C', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) E = 40 × 100 + 0.040 × 100² = 4400 µV. (b) E = 40 × 50 + 0.040 × 50² = 2100 µV. (c) linear reading = 2100 ÷ 4400 × 100 = 47.7 °C. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: substitution at 100 °C. A1: 4400 µV. A1: 2100 µV. C1: proportion of the interval. A1: θ = 47.7 °C.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgc9d63258-t fgc9d63258-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgc9d63258-t">Thermocouple e.m.f.</title><desc id="fgc9d63258-d">Graph of thermocouple e.m.f. E = aθ + bθ² against temperature from 0 to 300 °C, with a = 40 µV K⁻¹ and b = 0.040 µV K⁻²: a curve that gets steeper.</desc><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="88.2" y1="34" x2="88.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="147" y1="34" x2="147" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="205.7" y1="34" x2="205.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="264.5" y1="34" x2="264.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d